      ":question/math-academy-id": "e-3634",
      ":question/problem": "Differentiate $x\\cos x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=\\cos x .$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\t (x\\cos x)' &=   u'(x) \\cdot v(x) + u(x) \\cdot v'(x)\\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t&= (x)'\\cdot \\cos x + x\\cdot (\\cos x)'\\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t   & = 1 \\cdot \\cos x + x (-\\sin x)\\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t  & =  \\cos x - x \\sin x\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
