        ":question/problem": "Differentiate ${e}^{x}(2+sin⁡(x)).$\n\n$({e}^{x}(2+sin⁡(x)))^{′}=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,{e}^{x}cos⁡(x)$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={e}^{x}$ and $v(x)=2+sin⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({e}^{x}sec⁡(x))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =({e}^{x})^{′}\\cdot (2+sin⁡(x))+{e}^{x}\\cdot (2+sin⁡(x))^{′} \\\\  & =({e}^{x})(2+sin⁡(x))+({e}^{x})(cos⁡(x)) \\\\  & =(2+sin⁡(x)){e}^{x}+{e}^{x}cos⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"
